 "Local skills. Examples included hunting and gathering forest produce. Skills reflected local surroundings and everyday needs.", "Family and community. In Sabah, children learnt from the people around them. Knowledge was shared through guidance and common experiences.", "Everyday skills. These included rice farming, animal rearing, carpentry, fishing and blowpipe skills. Other skills included hunting and climbing.", "The aim of education. Children were prepared to become independent adults. Education therefore helped prepare younger generations for adult life."], "text": "Oral stories. In Sarawak, stories conveyed ethnic practices and beliefs. This description concerns the particular ethnic context being discussed. Local skills. Examples included hunting and gathering forest produce. Skills reflected local surroundings and everyday needs. Family and community. In Sabah, children learnt from the people around them. Knowledge was shared through guidance and common experiences. Everyday skills. These included rice farming, animal rearing, carpentry, fishing and blowpipe skills. Other skills included hunting and climbing. The aim of education. Children were prepared to become independent adults. Education therefore helped prepare younger generations for adult life."}